posts.body:
You can turn off the shop status window in plugin settings.
Battle Scene Settings - General - Show Shop Stauts?
For the other things you can put this as a plugin below VS (copy paste to notepad, save as .js file and add as plugin).
You might need to add/subtract from the x values.
const _myEdit1_SceneBattle_updateFrontviewBattleUiPositions = Scene_Battle.prototype.updateFrontviewBattleUiPositions;
Scene_Battle.prototype.updateFrontviewBattleUiPositions = function() {
_myEdit1_SceneBattle_updateFrontviewBattleUiPositions.call(this);
this._itemWindow.x = this._actorCommandWindow.x + this._actorCommandWindow.width;
this._itemWindow.y = this._actorCommandWindow.y;
this._skillWindow.x = this._actorCommandWindow.x + this._actorCommandWindow.width;
this._skillWindow.y = this._actorCommandWindow.y;
}
Window_BattleItem.prototype.maxCols = function() {
return 2;
};
However, that might cause a bit of a 1 frame flash in some instances when the window moves for some reason. If you want to get rid of that, I think it works if you write that method name in the console and get the obfuscated method and try to comment out lines until you find the one that moves the item or skill windows and make a plugin out of that.

